cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this artifact, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "ORM query performance across four database systems: public code and measurements"
abstract: >-
  Public artifact for How Portable Is ORM Query Performance? Evidence from Four
  Database Systems. Includes Django and SQLAlchemy query implementations,
  measurement harnesses, and reproducible analysis of PostgreSQL, MySQL, Oracle
  and Commercial System A at scale factor 1. All 432 planned cells remain in the
  coverage grid, including 336 measured analytical comparisons and 80 measured
  transactional comparisons. All measurements and full four-system results are
  retained; Commercial System A uses an anonymous label in the data and analysis.
  The manuscript is not yet published.
